nd post-acquisition MRI data quality control",0,17,"2016-08-01T10:13:10.000Z",1,12,20,0,0,["https://github.com/CyclotronResearchCentre/MRIquality/wiki"],11,1,"CyclotronResearchCentre/MRIquality",8,4,0,0,6,0,"2021-09-20T12:02:10.000Z",null,null,"MRIquality MRIquality is a collection of tools for routine quality assurance (QA) and post-acquisition MRI data quality control (QC). It currently includes mainly tools for EPI data (including fMRI and DWI acquisitions). Visit the Wiki for more details on the implemented tools."],["github:dankessler/umichneuroimaging",0,"dankessler/UMichNeuroimaging","https://github.com/dankessler/UMichNeuroimaging","Website for UMich Neuroimaging campuswide community",0,18,"2016-08-11T20:44:54.000Z",8,13,21,0,0,[],0,2,"dankessler/UMichNeuroimaging",0,0,0,0,11,0,"2016-08-11T20:46:24.000Z",null,null,""],["github:dhanzhang/weasis",0,"dhanzhang/Weasis","https://github.com/dhanzhang/Weasis","Weasis is a DICOM viewer available as a desktop application (no need to be installed, can be used on removable devices) or as a web-based application.",0,19,"2016-08-19T08:24:04.000Z",12,14,22,0,0,[],10,3,"dhanzhang/Weasis",0,0,0,0,5,0,"2021-03-10T01:39:29.000Z",null,null,""],["github:edwardtyantov/ultrasound-nerve-segmentation",0,"EdwardTyantov/ultrasound-nerve-segmentation","https://github.com/EdwardTyantov/ultrasound-nerve-segmentation","Kaggle Ultrasound Nerve Segmentation competition [Keras]",0,20,"2016-08-19T06:07:18.000Z",13,15,23,0,0,["https://github.com/jocicmarko/ultrasound-nerve-segmentation/"],1,1,"EdwardTyantov/ultrasound-nerve-segmentation",181,58,4,0,0,0,"2018-06-29T11:24:44.000Z",null,null,"Ultrasound nerve segmentation using Keras (1.0.7) Kaggle Ultrasound Nerve Segmentation competition [Keras] Install (Ubuntu {14,16}, GPU) cuDNN required. Theano - http://deeplearning.net/software/theano/install_ubuntu.html#install-ubuntu - sudo pip install pydot-ng In ~/.theanorc ``` [global] device = gpu0 [dnn] enabled = True ``` Keras - sudo apt-get install libhdf5-dev - sudo pip install h5py - sudo pip install pydot - sudo pip install nose_parameterized - sudo pip install keras In ~/.keras/keras.json (it's very important, the project was running on theano backend, and some issues are possible in case of TensorFlow) ``` { \"image_dim_ordering\": \"th\", \"epsilon\": 1e-07, \"floatx\": \"float32\", \"backend\": \"theano\" } ``` Python deps - sudo apt-get install python-opencv - sudo apt-get install python-sklearn Prepare Place train and test data into "],["github:emsweene/neuro_wave_bergen",0,"emsweene/neuro_wave_bergen","https://github.com/emsweene/neuro_wave_bergen","Setup for using common neuroimaging software on the wave and bergen servers at Rice.",0,21,"2016-08-28T20:40:17.000Z",2,13,24,0,0,[],0,2,"emsweene/neuro_wave_bergen",0,0,0,0,11,0,"2016-08-31T20:37:42.000Z",null,null,""],["github:ericspod/eidolon",0,"ericspod/Eidolon","https://github.com/ericspod/Eidolon","Biomedical Visualization and Analysis Framework",0,22,"2016-08-15T17:23:39.000Z",1,2,25,7,0,["https://ericspod.github.io/Eidolon/"],12,5,"ericspod/Eidolon",42,7,1,5,0,0,"2024-01-12T01:16:16.000Z",null,null,""],["github:funduscamera/raspberrypi",0,"FundusCamera/raspberrypi","https://github.com/FundusCamera/raspberrypi","Fundus Camera implementation using Raspberry Pi 3 and Raspberry Pi Camera Module. Concept by Dr Hong Sheng Chiong",0,23,"2016-08-03T14:45:36.000Z",7,16,26,0,0,[],13,2,"FundusCamera/raspberrypi",0,0,0,0,11,0,"2016-08-03T14:45:37.000Z",null,null,""],["github:githxt/imagej",0,"GitHXT/ImageJ","https://github.com/GitHXT/ImageJ","Batch cell counting - Confocal microscopy",0,24,"2016-08-08T02:55:14.000Z",1,17,27,0,0,[],5,4,"GitHXT/ImageJ",0,0,0,0,11,0,"2016-08-08T03:24:30.000Z",null,null,""],["github:gjcooper/uon-mrcourse-2016",0,"gjcooper/UoN-MRCourse-2016","https://github.com/gjcooper/UoN-MRCourse-2016","Talk on fMRI for Radiographers and Radiologists for UoN Magnetic Resonance Course Oct 2016",0,25,"2016-08-09T03:20:29.000Z",14,18,28,0,0,[],